          "code": "RSV_FLOW_REPORT_STATUS",
          "id": "1774155019024",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774155019025_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Role: Warehouse Manager\n\nTask:\nReview the “Create Reservation” REST API execution details and provide a short, business-friendly status update for a business user (no technical jargon unless necessary).\n\nInputs:\n- API Response Payload: {{$context.$nodes.ALLOC_EXECUTE_REQUEST.$output}}\n- Error (if any): {{$context.$error}}\n\nInstructions:\n1) Determine the overall outcome:\n   - If an error is present in {{$context.$error}} OR the response indicates failure → Status = “Failed”.\n   - If the response indicates success (e.g., reservation created/accepted) → Status = “Successful”.\n   - If the outcome is unclear → Status = “Pending/Needs Review”.\n\n2) Extract and summarize (when available) the key business details:\n   - Reservation status / result\n   - Reservation ID / reference number\n   - Order / shipment / wave / allocation identifiers (if present)\n   - Item(s) and quantities reserved (high level)\n   - Warehouse / facility and location (if present)\n\n3) If Failed:\n   - Provide a plain-language reason for the failure (translate technical errors into business impact).\n   - Include the next action (e.g., “retry”, “validate inventory”, “check order holds”, “contact IT/support”), based on the error type.\n\n4) If Successful:\n   - Confirm what was reserved and any immediate operational impact (e.g., “inventory is now committed for picking”).\n\n5) Output format (keep to 4–8 lines):\n   - Subject line\n   - Status (Successful / Failed / Pending)\n   - Key details (2–4 bullets)\n   - Next step (1 line)\n\nNow generate the business-facing status update using the provided inputs."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
