          "convergenceTargetId": "1774419913175",
          "id": "1774354169551",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774354169553_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Input: {{$context.$nodes.Init_actions_prepare_data.$output.result}}\n\nContext:\nWe are creating a supply request for a lot that is expiring soon in another organization.\n\nTask:\nFor each row in the input array, create one critical/high priority action to create a supply request.\n\nAction requirements (per row):\n- Title: \"Create Supply Request for expiring lot of <item> from <source_org> to <requesting_org>\"\n  - <item>: derive from the row’s item identifier/name (use the best available item-related field in the row)\n  - <source_org>: the organization where the expiring lot currently resides (use the best available source/supplying org field)\n  - <requesting_org>: the organization that needs the supply (use the best available destination/requesting org field)\n  - If you cannot confidently distinguish source vs requesting org from the row, use:\n    \"Create Supply Request for expiring lot of <item> from <org>\"\n- Description: must include demand details AND expiring-lot details from the row, including as available:\n  - demand qty, UOM, need-by/date, requester/customer/project, source info\n  - lot number, expiration date, on-hand/available qty, and any relevant subinventory/locator\n- Set the priority attribute to true.\n\nAction invocation (per row):\nAction - ora.Agent({\n  \"command\": \"expiryAction_CR_SUP_REQ\",\n  \"subAgent\": \"INV_WH_OPS_LOT_EXPIRATION_AGENT\",\n  \"agent\": \"INV_WH_OPS_ITEM_QUANTITY_MONITOR\",\n  \"parameters\": {\n  \"documentIdentifier\":  <documentIdentifier>\n}\n})\n\n\n\nRules:\n- Create exactly one action per row.\n- Do not drop, rename, or transform any fields in the row object when embedding it in parameters.row.\n- If a field needed for <item> / <source_org> / <requesting_org> is missing, use the best available alternative field from the row; if none exist, use \"Unknown Item\" / \"Unknown Org\"."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
